          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many calories are in a scoop of protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most standard scoops have 100 to 140 calories; the median whey isolate in our database lists 110 and the median plant blend 150. Meal shakes and greens blends run higher, around 180 to 250. Mass gainers are in another league, often 1,200 calories or more per serving, so read the panel if the tub is a gainer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use a measuring cup instead of the scoop?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, as a rough guide. A quarter cup is close to one serving for many whey powders and a third of a cup for bulkier plant blends, but density varies. For accuracy, weigh the labeled grams on a kitchen scale once, see how full the cup gets, and use that level from then on."
          }
