        <div id="protein-per-scoop" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. How Much Protein Is in a Scoop of Protein Powder?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Most single-scoop servings give 20 to 25 grams of protein, and the median is 24 grams. The share of the powder that is actually protein is the more useful number: across our standard labels the median is about 73 percent, so a 31 gram scoop holds roughly 22 to 23 grams of protein and the rest is flavor, sweetener, carbohydrate, fat and minerals.
          </p>

          <p>
            That percentage separates the types more cleanly than scoop size does. A good unflavored whey isolate can reach 80 to 90 percent protein by weight: NOW Sports Whey Isolate lists 24 grams of protein in 28 grams. Flavored blends usually land in the 70s. Plant blends with greens or superfoods often fall to 50 or 60 percent; Orgain's plant powder lists 21 grams of protein in a 46 gram, two-scoop serving, about 46 percent.
          </p>

